{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred","id":1098854,"title":"15th generation Kindred","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T13:08:18-07:00","id":1098854,"title":"15th generation Kindred","content":"Since 15th generation Kindred are the only Kindred with canon examples of fertility, they are the only generation of Kindred that can produce Dhampir children according to canon. Since sex is commonly used to disguise feeding among the Kindred, 15th generation Kindred would have plenty of opportunity to impregnate or get pregnant by their mortal lovers (especially since they would require multiple partners during a week). With average human fertility levels and average contraceptive use, male 15th generation Kindred who used sex to disguise feeding would impregnate an average of two mortal women per year while female 15th generation Kindred who used sex to disguise feeding would have an average of one pregnancy by a mortal man per year. Since there are probably 12,000 15th generation Kindred in existence by my calculation and since 50% of them probably use sex to disguise feeding, that would mean that there would be an average of over 9,000 Dhampir being born in Kindred-held territory every year since 2000. My questions are how noticeable would the birth of that many Dhampir be to mortal authorities and what effect would that many 15th generation Kindred have on Kindred society (especially since they would likely have numerous Dhampir children under their guidance)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:21:57-07:00","id":1098861,"title":"","content":"I personally think that the creation of Dhampir wouldn't register too much given how spread out Kindred are. In Kindred society, I'd almost think that they'd be lower than Caitiff due to how thin the blood has become to facilitate their births. In fact, I wouldn't be surprised if many were exterminated, especially in regions where the destruction of high Generation Kindred is common. A huge part of keeping the Masquerade has been population control, so I could see it being carried to a logical extreme very easily. If it was a pregnant 15th Gen, a forcible abortion or termination of the mother doesn't seem too far fetched. For those with a Kindred father, it'd be a bit more difficult to track, but if it became obvious that some kid growing up somewhere is exhibiting certain traits, I'm sure it wouldn't go unnoticed. <br /> <br /> Also, where's your math coming from? I'm very curious. Also, the birthrate seems rather high given the existence of contraceptives, birth control, and abortion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13249-sandcarlyle","name":"SandCarlyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:41:12-07:00","id":1098871,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain that 15th generation vampires can <i>occasionally</i> produce children. They aren't anywhere close to as fertile as humans.<br /> <br /> I also think 12,000 15th generation kindred is fairly optimistic as well. I thought that when 13th and 14th gens attempted to sire, it failed and simply killed the person more often than not. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:00:01-07:00","id":1098884,"title":"","content":"I'd agree. 15th generation vampires are supposed to be a recent development\u2014the curse has only just thinned/adapted enough to support them coming back as vampires in the past few decades, and I don't get the impression they're all that common yet. While there are probably a number of dhampirs at this point rather than it being a singular, portentous occurrence like it was in the Revised game, I don't see hordes of them running around endangering the masquerade. They'd probably blend into the general population of kids and teens with anger management issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:03:39-07:00","id":1098886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 15th generation vampires are supposed to be a recent development </div> </div> </div>I dunno... The only difference between 10th gen Sabbat and 15th gen Sabbat is a mere 5 successive failed cannonfodder waves and mass embraces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5520-hideamuro","name":"Hideamuro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:11:20-07:00","id":1098890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1098871#post1098871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain that 15th generation vampires can <i>occasionally</i> produce children. They aren't anywhere close to as fertile as humans.<br /> <br /> I also think 12,000 15th generation kindred is fairly optimistic as well. I thought that when 13th and 14th gens attempted to sire, it failed and simply killed the person more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>, your numbers presume a lot that isn't backed up by the books.<br /> <br /> 14th Gens embracing fails a good deal of the time, and they're at least somewhat rare as Vampires go from what I remember. Using the 12,000 number, you think 15th Gens comprise 17% of the global Vampire (Kindred and Kuei jin) population?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:22:20-07:00","id":1098895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hideamuro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1098886#post1098886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno... The only difference between 10th gen Sabbat and 15th gen Sabbat is a mere 5 successive failed cannonfodder waves and mass embraces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh what? Shovel heads don't get to embrace the next wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:02:39-07:00","id":1098910,"title":"","content":"I use a ratio of 1:100,000 as the global population of Kindred because that results in a ratio of 1:50,000 in Africa, Europe, North America, South America, West Asia and a third of South Asia (the KJ would have a global ratio of 1:100,000, giving them a ratio of 1:50,000 in East Asian, Southeast Asia, and two-thirds of South Asia, giving the Kindred and KJ roughly equivalent populations). The majority of the 15th generation would be in Sub-saharan Africa, since the default canon generation is 14th according to KotEK, and forty percent of the Kindred seem to live in Sub-Saharan Africa (I do not like KotEK, but it is canon, so I use the figures). The figure of 12,000 is just based off a simple extrapolation of the existent population of 13th generation Kindred in 1e (in 1992, 13th generation was the default generation and 15th generation existed, though their special rules came much later). Using Revised numbers (rather than extrapolating from 1e and 2e numbers), we would reduce 15th and Dhampir populations by one-third, which would still result in 90,000 Dhampir born from 2000 to 2015.<br /> <br /> Human fertility averages one pregnancy every forty unprotected sexual acts, Kindred do not normally need contraception so most sexual acts would likely be unprotected (when their victim experiences the Kiss, they will not notice the diffrrence) and only 50% of women in developed countries are on chemical birth control. While abortion is a possibility, the legality, availability, and accessibility varies from nation to nation, so I estimate that only 25% would be aborted. If another 25% terminate due to complications, the result is 2 Dhampir sired per year, assuming one feeding per day. It may be higher in developing nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 05-31-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:53:48-07:00","id":1100477,"title":"","content":"Technically a 15th gen with a blood pool of six only needs to feed about twice a week, assuming a sedentary NPC lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Dhampir are first introduced as playable in Time of Thin Blood, released in 1999. If we assume that a viable PC Dhampir is at least in their late teens* and that the release of the book also coincides with Dhampir numbers reaching a level that an awareness of them as a phenomenon exists* then one can also assume that 15th generation vampires must have begun emerging around the late 70's to early 80's.<br /> <br /> *Child characters are a thing but we shouldn't treat them as the default.<br /> <br /> **There's nothing stopping you from playing one in an earlier time period but if we accept that Dhampir are a new and scary thing then it makes as much sense as anything to use the release of the book detailing them as their point of emergence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 06-05-2017, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:11:17-07:00","id":1100482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1100477#post1100477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically a 15th gen with a blood pool of six only needs to feed about twice a week, assuming a sedentary NPC lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Dhampir are first introduced as playable in Time of Thin Blood, released in 1999. If we assume that a viable PC Dhampir is at least in their late teens* and that the release of the book also coincides with Dhampir numbers reaching a level that an awareness of them as a phenomenon exists* then one can also assume that 15th generation vampires must have begun emerging around the late 70's to early 80's.<br /> <br /> *Child characters are a thing but we shouldn't treat them as the default.<br /> <br /> **There's nothing stopping you from playing one in an earlier time period but if we accept that Dhampir are a new and scary thing then it makes as much sense as anything to use the release of the book detailing them as their point of emergence.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a blood pool of 10, not 6. They can only spend 6 of their blood points on things other than Rising in the evening, true (I think they can spend the last 4 on a few other things too) and 1 BP for them costs 2 BP (jesus they are underpowered, but I guess that's the point), but they do have 10 BP really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:13:51-07:00","id":1100484,"title":"","content":"Side Note: I have a 15th Generation NPC in my game, and she has Insight at 5. She figures out a lot of stuff the PCs miss, but only if it relates to Kindred. One PC became over-reliant on her sight, and ran into a human she had almost killed (her old GF and roommate) and whose memory she had wiped. Obviously she's upset by seeing her again, and she blames the NPC for not warning her about her being there. I had a response ready: &quot;I'm not a God Ruli. I can only see those who are linked to the power of the blood, and trying to use me as a universal alarm system will be your undoing if you aren't careful.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T11:56:35-07:00","id":1100519,"title":"","content":"Probably a fringe opinion but personally I run that there are no thin bloods so 14th generation and up works just like 13th generation. The only real difference is that its a lot harder to use diablerie to get to a lower generation with more power to it. Never was a fan of the thin blood concept to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T15:08:38-07:00","id":1100607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1100519#post1100519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a fringe opinion but personally I run that there are no thin bloods so 14th generation and up works just like 13th generation. The only real difference is that its a lot harder to use diablerie to get to a lower generation with more power to it. Never was a fan of the thin blood concept to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read Time of Thin Blood? One of the best VTM books in my opinion. It is about the state of vampirism itself more than anything, thin bloods are just a really interesting case that the book focuses on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T21:21:19-07:00","id":1100697,"title":"","content":"I love how in JHD Netchurch is trying to breed a Dhampir and a Revenant because of course he is.... he's like a PC npc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T22:41:36-07:00","id":1100718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1100607#post1100607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you read Time of Thin Blood? One of the best VTM books in my opinion. It is about the state of vampirism itself more than anything, thin bloods are just a really interesting case that the book focuses on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid that I can't say that I have read thart one. If I read it I may well change my opinion, but with so many books on the &quot;i want to read&quot; list I don't think that its going to happen anytime soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T23:56