coming back from that bliss. before he/she realise she's(the vampire) already gone.<br /> <br /> To me when they say vampire uses sex to feed, this is what they are referring to, and not the actual act, at the very least most of the time in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:02:16-07:00","id":1102001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102000#post1102000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First like SandCarlyle pointed out there is birth control, secondly most and like 90% if not all my vampire would not go further than foreplay and even then, I can't imagine that most vampire (not all) - aside from maybe those with higher humanity, the nympho, or simply those in love that will still go through it from principale. I can't imagine most vampire being actually interested in making love. It clearly state in the book that vampire have lost their libido, that alone, I think that would already greatly lessen the chance of a vampire actually going through the act, also it is suggested that all fuild is blood and so the men ejaculation and women squirt would make a bloody mess pun intended<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I would believe that once that happens most(not all obviously) would refrain from going through that again.<br /> <br /> Also, in most situation I imagine what a typical feeding process would look like; (of any common female vampire for example would be<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Female vampire goes into a bar, looks at one of the dude or dudette, with a smile, a look that she may be an easy girl, guys/gal walk to the vampire ask her if he/she can buy her a drink, she goes straight to the point, refuses but ask him/her if he/she is interested in going some place more quiet, they leave the bar, goes into the nearest alley/backstreet, kiss, make out, girl either goes for his/her neck or ask him/her to close his eyes or whatever and then bites the fools, drink a little of his/her blood, the guy/gal goes to heaven, best make out he/she ever had, Vampire lick the wound close, and leave the poor dude/dudette who is still coming back from that bliss. before he/she realise she's(the vampire) already gone.<br /> <br /> To me when they say vampire uses sex to feed, this is what they are referring to, and not the actual act, at the very least most of the time in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're 15th Generation they WILL crave sex the way humans do. They randomly grow stubble, go through the menstrual cycle, make saliva, cry real tears... and they can deliberately trigger it with blood. This means that the factors that drive us to have sex will effect thin-bloods. When they have sex genuine ejaculation can happen by accident. If a 15th Generation kindred is sexually active, there is a decent chance of them producing a Dhampir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:13:33-07:00","id":1102007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102001#post1102001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they're 15th Generation they WILL crave sex the way humans do. They randomly grow stubble, go through the menstrual cycle, make saliva, cry real tears... and they can deliberately trigger it with blood. This means that the factors that drive us to have sex will effect thin-bloods. When they have sex genuine ejaculation can happen by accident. If a 15th Generation kindred is sexually active, there is a decent chance of them producing a Dhampir.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they are, than I think that most would use contraceptive unless in an area where such is illegal and/or unavailable, in which case the Dhampir may be born, but all in all, I imagine the 15th Gen to be almost non-existant and at the most not more than 1000 on the planet, and I would probably go for a lot less in any of my game, like recent phenomena and less than 50 world wide, and I would have the Camarilla Elder on a secret agenda to make sure that such being does not live very long, mostly out of fear of thin blood and what it means (gehenna and all that). I would expect the dhampir population if we can even call them that, to be within the 10 to 20 maximum. I don't believe that there is enough that they could be a small village full of them (Blade (*marvel) -like character going around killing shit. Also as for as I am concerned they would be hunted by the Inquisition, the Vampire and the Garou, as well as any vampire hunter, that is enough to reduce your chance of survival to the minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:19:49-07:00","id":1102009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102007#post1102007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they are, than I think that most would use contraceptive unless in an area where such is illegal and/or unavailable, in which case the Dhampir may be born, but all in all, I imagine the 15th Gen to be almost non-existant and at the most not more than 1000 on the planet, and I would probably go for a lot less in any of my game, like recent phenomena and less than 50 world wide, and I would have the Camarilla Elder on a secret agenda to make sure that such being does not live very long, mostly out of fear of thin blood and what it means (gehenna and all that). I would expect the dhampir population if we can even call them that, to be within the 10 to 20 maximum. I don't believe that there is enough that they could be a small village full of them (Blade (*marvel) -like character going around killing shit. Also as for as I am concerned they would be hunted by the Inquisition, the Vampire and the Garou, as well as any vampire hunter, that is enough to reduce your chance of survival to the minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so a 15th Generation Kindred impregnates a random hookup. They don't get birth control, or can't, and give birth to a Dhampir. There is no way to differentiate them from normal children which would actually reduce their survival rate. If they are found, they will be assumed as a Lost Revenant; there is a whole foundation (The Romanian Legacy Foundation) devoted to finding lost children of the blood.<br /> <br /> I imagine that in 2017 there would be fewer than 100 Dhampir in the whole world, yes, but that's only because there are so few 15th Generation kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:30:21-07:00","id":1102012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred#post1098854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since sex is commonly used to disguise feeding among the Kindred, 15th generation Kindred would have plenty of opportunity to impregnate or get pregnant by their mortal lovers (especially since they would require multiple partners during a week).<br /> <br /> With average human fertility levels<br /> <br /> since 50% of them probably use sex to disguise feeding</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the biggest gripes I have. Even going with old numbers (1E, 2E, Revised, etc) we start with a couple weird ideas.<br /> -That these 15th generation have multiple partners. They might have a very fixed herd.<br /> -That we should be using average human fertility levels. Not sure if that is justified here.<br /> -What amount of 15th generation would still decide to use contraception, especially after they probably find out they got someone pregnant.<br /> -That 50% of them even use sex to disguise feeding as a means.<br /> +Relating to multiple partners, even if they use sex for feeding, how often they use other methods instead.<br /> -That these 15th generation Kindred are even finishing their sexual encounters in a way that would lead to pregnancy.<br /> <br /> Again, all this even making the assumption on how many 15th generation exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:32:51-07:00","id":1102013,"title":"","content":"Man, I should make friends with these 15th gen kindred that are apparently all polygamist sex gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:36:46-07:00","id":1102015,"title":"","content":"Well I guess it depends on how far reaching you give the Camarilla power, in my game , as a Storyteller, I always went that the Camarilla Alone, have prevented the world from finding out that the Vampire actually exist, and part of the reason why they were able to do that, is because, they are everywhere, virtually almost every institution on the planet is either watch or have been infiltrate by either allies or ghoul or member of the Sect. If there is an institution that track and care and attempt to protect such children so call lost children of the blood, the Camarilla would either be able to muscle it , and often destroy some of their instition and these unfortunate souls they are protecting. And/or either buy the information on their whereabouts and then send anyone really, they could arrange for hunters to stumble on their track, or make it so that a pack of garou thinks that they are a threat or send a sheriff, there is really a dozen ways they could go about making sure that their number remains low, at the very least.<br /> <br /> I don't except the Camarilla would be able to track all of them down (obviously) but I except them to be a major reason why there are not more of them aside from the fact that there is not alot of 15 gen. Also the fact that with all of that being said, I would expect most of them (hating what they are, hating vampires and) to become vampire hunter, and because of that, obviously expediting their expiration date <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:38:51-07:00","id":1102018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102013#post1102013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I should make friends with these 15th gen kindred that are apparently all polygamist sex gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Vampires are sexy, thanks to the Kiss, and a 15th Generation is a Vampire who is warm to the touch, blushes, still gets tingles, and just feels alive. I think out of all the possibilities on the table, a 15th Generation Cainite is pretty sexy. Plus they won't have stable herds, and they're young, so feeding on hookups will be a relatively popular method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:56:43-07:00","id":1102024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102018#post1102018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Vampires are sexy, thanks to the Kiss, and a 15th Generation is a Vampire who is warm to the touch, blushes, still gets tingles, and just feels alive. I think out of all the possibilities on the table, a 15th Generation Cainite is pretty sexy. Plus they won't have stable herds, and they're young, so feeding on hookups will be a relatively popular method.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is assuming they all have either the skills or disciplines to facilitate said hookups. Tom Pander, 67 year old mailman with two kids and a beer gut, might very well be a loser with no social ability and all his dots in Fortitude (no offense to mailmen or people named Tom). They aren't sexy because of the Kiss. The Kiss allows the act itself to go well (generally speaking). But it isn't what's ensuring all these encounters happen in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm just not buying there are 1. a lot of 15th generation, 2. that they are all these pickup artists having lots of unprotected sex with numerous partners, 3. that many even result in births for several reasons.<br /> <br /> If we're being really technical, the estimations on birth control and abortion probably vary a lot depending on the demographic. The type of person having hookups is probably a lot more likely to be watching out for that sort of thing, I'd think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T10:52:10-07:00","id":1102037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102024#post1102024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is assuming they all have either the skills or disciplines to facilitate said hookups. Tom Pander, 67 year old mailman with two kids and a beer gut, might very well be a loser with no social ability and all his dots in Fortitude (no offense to mailmen or people named Tom). They aren't sexy because of the Kiss. The Kiss allows the act itself to go well (generally speaking). But it isn't what's ensuring all these encounters happen in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm just not buying there are 1. a lot of 15th generation, 2. that they are all these pickup artists having lots of unprotected sex with numerous partners, 3. that many even result in births for several reasons.<br /> <br /> If we're being really technical, the estimations on birth control and abortion probably vary a lot depending on the demographic. The type of person having hookups is probably a lot more likely to be watching out for that sort of thing, I'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the examples of 15th Gen I've seen are very young, since the creators clearly wanted to associate them with youth thematically speaking. The oldest I can think of is Vampire Dad from Time of Thin Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:09:42-07:00","id":1102044,"title":"","content":"You're assuming a half-dead thing with some semi-functional biology has equivalent fertility to a healthy human being. 15th gen Fertilization success rates and embryo maturation success rates could be 1% or less of human, for all we know. You're also assuming that seduction feedings all terminate in sex (rather than just biting when the opportunity presents itself e..g making out or something), that Thin Bloods aren't weighted towards being marginalized creatures forced disproportionately to feed off of family, animals, or vagrants, and that the Thin Blood bothers to fulfill the act of sex unto orgasm rather than just, again, engaging the Kiss when he/she has the subject in a compromised position.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 06-09-2017, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:21:13-07:00","id":1102047,"title":"","content":"If 15th generation male Kindred have male human hormones, why would they not finish the sexual act? Heck, it is not like their partner would actually care if they were not wearing a condom if their partner is experiencing the Kiss. Biting is common in sex, and a 15th generation male Kindred could get a reputation as a phenomenal lover if he times the Kiss just right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:38:28-07:00","id":1102058,"title":"","content":"They still aren't actually human anymore. I would imagine that most of their drives are still sublimated into the urge to feed, just as with other kindred; the ability to ejaculate sperm with finite viability does mean that you actually have a strong sex drive, especially if you're hooking up purely with the intention of scoring blood to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:10:03-07:00","id":1102066,"title":"","content":"It is not that hard to make a 15th generation male that is capable of using sex for feeding in V20 (and I imagine that combining the two sensations would be very desirable and very addictive) just by taking the 15th generation Flaw [-4] and constructing the character according to the normal character creation rules, probably giving him Friendly Face [1] and Enchanting Voice [2] to give him a -3 difficulty on seduction rolls. Every night, the character would go out and feed on a woman after picking her up at a bar, and the character would likely not realize that he could get the woman pregnant because he thinks that he is infertile because he is a vampire. With Fortitude 3 and Stamina 4, he could actually deal with incidental sunlight without suffering that much lethal damage and could probably make a living through working during the day as long as he did not take that many risks and kept a high enough Humanity (8+).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:13:34-07:00","id":1102068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102066#post1102066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not that hard to make a 15th generation male that is capable of using sex for feeding in V20</div> </div> </div> </div> Kind of besides the point. Just because it is easy to do so mechanically as a storyteller/player, doesn't mean it is a likely average character to be produced in the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:30:08-07:00","id":1102071,"title":"","content":"Young vampires who use sex for feeding are practically archetypal characters in contemporary urban fantasy novels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:49:54-07:00","id":1102076,"title":"","content":"Even with seven soak dice, he'd be provoking a lethal damage soak roll every 5 seconds when exposed to appreciable amounts of sunlight; hardly sustainable for even several hours, statistically.<br /> <br /> Just because it is an archetype does not mean it is a statistically common outcome for 15th generation vampires in this setting. This also assumes that the partners have average rates of contraceptive usage; my suspicion is that susceptible bar/nightclub goers have much higher rates of birth control usage than the average American etc. female. Likewise, probability of morning after/abortion recourse seem higher after cognizance of unprotected sex or association of a pregnancy with a one night stand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 06-09-2017, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:44:39-07:00","id":1102094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1102066#post1102066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not that hard to make a 15th generation male that is capable of using sex for feeding in V20</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point you are designing a character (mechanically) around your proposed &quot;common&quot; concept of how 15th gens feed.<br /> <br /> That you feel the need to do so kind of refutes your own initial concept/question. These sorts of instances are just not that common.<br /> <br /> And the WoD setting is very different from most &quot;contemporary urban fantasy novels&quot; settings. For one, a character like this is all but guaranteed a short unlife due to the in setting vampire power structures. This character would be lucky to survive just a few months I would think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:01:19-07:00","id":1102131,"title":"","content":"Actually I could see 15th gens and the like being any age and background for a simple reason...<br /> <br /> They're a mistake.<br /> <br /> Some 14th gen Caitif, unaware of the traditions and on the run. Grabs some guy in a bit of frenzy and sucks him dry. &quot;Wait, wait.... there's something about feedign them blood to heal them right? I read that somewhere?&quot; Drops some blood in. Nothing happens. panics and runs off. a little later, (or a lot later...) the 15th gen wakes up. <br /> <br /> This could be a plot point to introduce the thin bloods in a game itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;What does Sherrif stick-uphis-butt want the enonates to do tonight?&quot;<br /> &quot;Got to go down to the morgue and do some masqurade cover-up. Apparently someone broken in stole a couple bodies and chowed down on the coroner. Simple dominate and presence fix. Need somebody to find the body jackers though.&quot;<br /> &quot;You know it was those Damn Giovanni.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, but better the new licks on the block than anyone important...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:12:10-07:00","id":1102138,"title":"","content":"I imagine that most of the 15th generations that survive will live in small cities (either they moved there after they were Embraced or they were Embraced by nomadic 14th generation Kindred). In a city with a population of 10,000 to 50,000, they might be the only Kindred in the entire city, allowing them to effectively rule the city despite their relative lack of supernatural power (Dominate 1-3 works just as well against Mortals whether the Kindred using it is 15th generation or 5th generation). If they augment their feeding on local humans with generous supplies of animal blood (a city of 10,000 will produce an average of 50 blood points worth of cow and pig blood per day), they should be able to survive without major issues as long as they are careful (one blood point per day from their human lovers and five blood points of cow and pig blood per day would probably be adequate). In the case of a 15th generation, the old saying applies, pigs get fat, hogs get slaughtered, and there are plenty of threats out there that can slaughtered a 15th generation hog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T00:46:40-07:00","id":1397016,"title":"","content":"Well in a V20 it whas even said as an Archetype for Caitiths to be a smalltown Prince because for those that survive they can harness the frontier and they do at least keep Autarkis and mayby fleeing Sabbat in bay. Another thing is I think with how fluctuate the fertility of Gen15+ cainit is I think the most Dhampirs are in the US. Because it is the country with the most sex rate of the Earth with each american having statistical every second day sex. I think there are enough idiots that are getting pregnant through One Night Stands and the health system there is still good enough to allow most of the childrens reach maturity.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another problem with the 15th generation is, that it is the first generation that comes way to soon. It needed nearly a millennium after the 13th generation for getting another generation and the 15th generation came up in a hundredth of time for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 06-17-2020, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T07:35:25-07:00","id":1397087,"title":"","content":"Arise, necro thread, arise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T07:44:33-07:00","id":1397089,"title":"","content":"Since the thread has reappeared, I'm going to drop out of stealth mode.<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>'s numbers are acceptable for kindred overall, though probably quite high for the number of fifteenth generation vampires... probably by an order of magnitude. Aya's numbers for human fertility pretty much match data for fertility among heterosexual, married couples who don't use birth control. One pregnancy per year for such couples is about right, historically. All this assuming they are having reproductive sex, of course. (ie Gay 15th gens aren't having accidental pregnancies.)<br /> <br /> I could quibble about the percent of kindred who feed using sex. Given V5 lists a dozen <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Predator_Type_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">predator types</a>, it might be about a tenth of vampire feedings overall.<br /> <br /> The fact remains that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>'s numbers can be quibbled with, but there <u>are</u> some dhampir in the world. <i>More than a small handful.</i><br /> <br /> Let's be very, very conservative with the numbers. Let's say:<ul><li>There are a thousand 15th generation vampires. About as many as a clan.</li> <li>Only a tenth of them (100 individuals) use the Siren method regularly.</li> <li>A third of those (33 individuals) regularly complete the act of reproductive sex, without <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prevalence_of_birth_control\" target=\"_blank\">birth control</a>.</li> <li>Those who do this have a similar reproductive rate to mundane humans, one birth per year.</li> <li>Except, according to ToTB, half of all such pregnancies end unsuccessfully. (So, about 16 per year.)</li> <li>This has been going on since 1999. (So, 300 dhampir exist.)</li> </ul><br /> Further, let's say, 2/3 of the children (200 dhampir) are being raised inside the Masquerade. By that I mean they are being reared in an environment which intentionally hides their existence from the public eye. This could be as simple as a mother who knows her ex-boyfriend is a vampire and knows to hide her child. This could also be a dhampir who has grown up in a Tremere chantry undergoing experiments. Point is, they are not available for public view.<br /> <br /> Let's say the other 1/3 are available for public view. This gives us a conservative estimate of 100 dhampir being raised by casual former sexual partners of a thin-blood, being raised by a family member of such a partner, or having passed into the adoption/foster care system.<br /> <br /> <u>Okay, so a (very conservative) total of 100 dhampir roaming unsupervised through human society. </u><br /> <br /> Now, onto the actual question at hand, as posted by Aya Tari.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My questions are how noticeable would the birth of that many Dhampir be to mortal authorities and what effect would that many 15th generation Kindred have on Kindred society (especially since they would likely have numerous Dhampir children under their guidance)? </div> </div> </div>The most important fact about dhampir for this discussion isn't their precise population numbers. It's that they are, mechanically, similar to Revenants. They have a dot in Potence, and a dot in another common discipline. They can heal wounds, including sometimes regrowing amputated limbs.<br /> <br /> Most important, they mature/age at 1/4 the normal rate, while remaining within age-appropriate parameters for their reduced age.<br /> <br /> So, there are 100 children who went to the pediatrician for a <a href=\"https://www.healthychildren.org/English/family-life/health-management/Pages/Well-Child-Care-A-Check-Up-for-Success.aspx\" target=\"_blank\">well-baby check-up</a> at one week, and presented as a three day old baby. Not unusual. The practitioner might suspect the due date was incorrect, and the baby was slightly premature. They might double-check the infant is feeding well, and prescribe supplements or breast feeding support. Overall, the medical system would watch and wait.<br /> <br /> As such check-ups continue an alarming pattern would emerge. At the age of one year, the child would have the cognitive and emotional development of a three-month-old. Not too unheard of; developmental disabilities are a known thing. Okay. Refer to specialists and start testing, testing, testing.<br /> <br /> But, there are 100 children who went at age four (around the time of pre-school) and had the physical, emotional, and cognitive development of an entirely healthy one-year-old.<br /> <br /> At eight, they will appear two years old. And so forth, until the oldest among the dhampir are now twenty years old and appear to be perfectly normal five-year-olds. Except, by now, they have shown super-strength, healing abilities, and at least one other discipline power. It will become clearer and clearer as time goes on that something previously undescribed is going on.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event it hasn't happened yet, there is no way I can imagine these children not being written up in a medical or educational journal, probably as an unexplained, rare syndrome. If there happen to be two unrelated dhampir identified, the floodgates will open as practitioners around the world put two-and-two together for their own dhampir.<br /> <br /> If anyone is inclined to quibble with the exact number of dhampir, fine, go ahead.<br /> <br /> But, somebody, please, also explain to me how they do not become <a href=\"https://abcnews.go.com/Health/maryland-20-year-dies-aged/story?id=20712718\" target=\"_blank\">public knowledge</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T08:45:26-07:00","id":1397098,"title":"","content":"Their slow maturing is slightly retconned by BJD. There it is said, Dhampirs are normal children until they reach puperty (though it is like normal children different when exectly this is) and their cainith legacy starts to show up. At this moment every Cainith will see, that the child is not totally human but physical it will be like it is a revenant., where normal humans react to him depending on his humanity number aka how much the beast has controll of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:05:51-07:00","id":1397431,"title":"","content":"The main issue I have with the original numbers is that it seems to assume that all *potential* pregnancies have a very high rate of success rather than a low. This seems unlikely to me, given that ghouls (as part of creating Revenants) often miscarry and it takes some very clever management (and no small amount of sorcery) to create enough ghouled-from-birth servants to breed said Revenants. Dhampir are functionally revenants and their parent is going to be under a similar stasis so I'd imagine they'd have it at least as bad as breeding ghouls (probably worse.)<br /> <br /> Indeed page 31 of ToTB mentions that there's a 20% chance of success (at best, or 'if all other factors are optimizied' as the book puts it) to impregnate (or for a vampire to get pregnant) IF they spend the requisite willpower and BP to 'reactivate' the needed anatomy. <br /> <br /> Even if conception occurs, there's about a 50% chance of carrying it to term rather than miscarrying (and the rules apply equally to a 15th generation mother or a mortal one) And its likely that the 50% chance is ALSO ideal circumstances since they ad the caveat 'assuming the conception, pregnancy, and birth take place unhindered' to the whole process. <br /> <br /> So at BEST you have a 1 in 10 chance of a 15th generation vampire producing a Dhampir under optimized circumstances. And if they're fucking around randomly as part of their feeding process, I kinda doubt any of that would qualify as 'optimized'. <br /> <br /> That said, this all also occurs without magic being involved, so I suspect if magic becomes a factor (like it does with Revenant creation) those chances could be modified (but use of said magic probably keeps them relatively rare the same it would for revenants.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T03:30:58-07:00","id":1397488,"title":"","content":"What TotB is saying too, that for 15th Generation cainites their sex drive is as low as for other vampires so it is not like every 15th generation just want really to have sex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T11:28:01-07:00","id":1397555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1098854-15th-generation-kindred?p=1397098#post1397098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their slow maturing is slightly retconned by BJD. There it is said, Dhampirs are normal children until they reach puperty (though it is like normal children different when exectly this is) and their cainith legacy starts to show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually is the same as when they were introduced in Time of Thin Blood. Dhampirs age at normal human rates until a post-puberty stressor causes their vampiric blood to kick in (which can be really annoying if it kicks in while being bullied at 13) and then slows to a crawl.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s, using half those previous numbers (because 15th gens aren\u2019t always fertile), 50 kids who mostly grow up like ordinary kids (they\u2019re said to be unusually quiet as infants, but extremely temperamental toddlers) until something bad happens... then they spontaneously develop super-strength and some other common discipline (so one of the less obvious ones), recover quick from injuries and all but stop aging (which, depending on the age, might not be all that noticeable... a thirty year old might look twenty if their vampiric nature kicked in at sixteen... it\u2019d be their late 40s to 50s before it starts getting obvious and some people just age well).<br /> <br /> Presuming half those kids are in smaller towns because that\u2019s where 15th gens are statistically safest... 25 of them live their whole lives as just the small town trouble-maker (who eventually graduates to a serious of dead-end jobs, failed relationships and trouble with the law because of their temper and inordinate strength) and not even be noticed for what they are (suicide, death by cop or similar other violent incident that goes the wrong way probably takes out quite a few before the slowed aging is notable. Some might not even have a trigger event their whole lives.<br /> <br /> 25 of them grow up in the city where a vampire MIGHT notice them... but again, not that noticeable given the disciplines they\u2019re likely to spontaneously develop (by the rules; auspex, celerity, dominate, fortitude, obfuscate or presence + potence) and more opportunities for death by unrelated violence due to their tempers.<br /> <br /> But even if all of them survive the mundane dangers of life that\u2019s still maybe two-dozen Dhampirs spread over the entire United States and a span of two decades who might wind up in a situation where they\u2019d be recognized by vampires as supernatural.<br /> <br /> And even then, the most likely means of doing so (Auspex) is probably going to identify them as a ghoul/revenant and further investigation would reveal a lack of an obvious master.<br /> <br /> Frankly, it\u2019s a minor miracle that the Camarilla is even aware Dhampirs exist (due to Dr. Netchurch\u2019s penchant for investigation instead of just disposing of a masterless ghoul without further investigation which I imagine would be the norm for Masquerade preservation).<br /> <br /> Outside of the 15-16th Gen parents, the average Cainite probably doesn\u2019t even know Dhampirs are possible (and the vamp parent still might not believe it). The average city has probably only ever had one Dhampir turn up and the odds of that one actually being recognized for what it actually is are rather slim; most probably got taken out without ever even knowing what they actually were.<br /> <br /> I think that\u2019s probably why Requiem tied in the notion that Dhampirs have some degree of supernatural luck simply to explain how enough of them exist to even BE a player character.<br /> <br /> So far, every Dhampir I\u2019ve ever made has had some type of \u201cgood\u201d fortune in their background that has allowed them to learn both what they are and a means to avoid being insta-ganked as a walking Masquerade violation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T20:22:12-07:00","id":1397613,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was in ToTB:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Time of Thin Blood page 48-49</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the thin-blooded are ignorant of their heritage, then how much more so are their mortal offspring? A dhampir\u2019s occult legacy usually doesn\u2019t manifest until the onset of puberty; in addition to all the usual tribulations of growing up, the child must face a second layer of transformation, far darker and infinitely more mysterious.<br /> <br /> The process varies from individual to individual. Most simply become aware, sometime during their teens, of a special reserve of physical strength that they can call upon \u2014 instinctively at first, in times of stress. They may be afraid of this power and the feral pleasure that accompanies using it, or they may be delighted to discover such a useful weapon against a harsh world and immediately set about finding its limits. Other dhampirs bloom later. For them, mystical dabbling or a sudden encounter with a vampire might be what it takes to spark their hidden potential.<br /> <br /> In any case, once a dhampir is fully awakened to her supernatural essence, she can never go back. The Blood forever alters her physically and mentally. Her aging slows to a crawl (which can be a real social disadvantage when it happens in early puberty). She gains a limited ability to learn vampiric Disciplines. She also gains an inner Beast, which, though mild compared to a vampire\u2019s, is still strong enough to test her heart and will. In other words, as Dr. Netchurch so astutely notes in Chapter One, she becomes biologically indistinguishable from a revenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the 'age normally until puberty' didn't start with BJD. The confusion may be from the fact Ghouls: Fatal Addiction notes that 'true' Revenants have slowed aging from birth (Netchurch notes this on page 22 of G:FA). Gestation (at least for Bratovich mothers) was 3 years and a revenant child took 50 years to reach puberty - which necessitated keeping them out of public sight or masking the slowed aging somehow. It was also allegedly why Revenants weren't more prolific given that adult Revenants had prolonged fertility for this same reason. Of course, this represents another major difference between Dhampir and Revenant even though they're 'biologically' indistinguishable from Revenants (And oddly one Netchurch could have noted but somehow missed.)<br /> <br /> Of course Revenants haven't been conceptually consistent either. The 'Ancient Revenants' who could live from 400-750 in 'Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand' (not to mention the Verbena-connected Rafiasto who had a small number of True Mages AND Thaumaturgy. Although as Revenants they can't have Numina which seems to include Hedge Magic.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 06-19-2020, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T01:35:12-07:00","id":1397639,"title":"","content":"As an alternative I don't like the idea of thinbloods so every vampire from 13th generation up are mechanically the same. High generation just means that you will be required to commit more juicy diableries in order get your generation lower to where its makes a mechanical effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}